  "chitchat": [
    "stirs the pot and watches the flats over your shoulder.",
    "\"Water's life out here. Don't waste mine.\"",
    "\"Camp's full. Doesn't mean you're welcome to stay.\""
  ],
  "description": "The matriarch of the Slake Pond camp: sun-cured, iron-grey, and entirely without illusions. She has buried more of her people than she'll say and guards the living with a pragmatism that shades into menace.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "accepted": {
      "actions": [
        {
          "action": "START_QUEST",
          "quest_id": "quest_bog_standard"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Understood.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"They den in the wet ground — the Seep, the Rust Marsh, the Runoff down south. Two at least. And mind your footing; the tar doesn't give anything back.\""
    },
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "\"Fill your jug and move on, then.\""
    },
    "quest_offer": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "I'll thin them out.",
          "next": "accepted"
        },
        {
          "label": "It's done. (report back)",
          "next": "reported"
        },
        {
          "label": "Not my fight.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Something's coming up out of the seeps — tar-things, big and slow and hungry. Took two of mine this week. Put a couple of them down and there's water, food, and goodwill in it. Goodwill's worth more than it sounds out here.\""
    },
    "reported": {
      "actions": [
        {
          "action": "TURN_IN",
          "quest_id": "quest_bog_standard"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Obliged.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"...The seeps are quieter. My people noticed. Here — clean water and a hot meal, and you're welcome at this fire, which is more than most get.\""
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "You run this camp?",
          "next": "quest_offer"
        },
        {
          "label": "Just passing through.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "A leather-faced woman looks up from a cook-pot, one hand never far from a length of pipe. \"This is my pond, my camp, my water. State your business or fill your jug and go.\""
    }
  },
